{"path":"/documentation/modeling/vllm/registration","section":"documentation","title":"registration","description":"Documentation for the nnsight Python library","toc":[{"id":"nnsight.modeling.vllm.registration","label":"registration","depth":2},{"id":"nnsight.modeling.vllm.registration.Registration","label":"Registration","depth":3},{"id":"nnsight.modeling.vllm.registration.ServeRegistration","label":"ServeRegistration","depth":3},{"id":"nnsight.modeling.vllm.registration.RegisteringTracer","label":"RegisteringTracer","depth":3}],"segments":[{"type":"html","html":"<h2 id=\"nnsight.modeling.vllm.registration\" class=\"doc-heading\">\n<code class=\"doc-symbol doc-symbol-heading doc-symbol-module\"></code>            <span class=\"doc-object-name doc-module-name\">registration</span>\n\n\n</h2>"},{"type":"html","html":"<p>Interventions that stay on the engine and run for every request.</p>\n<p>A trace ships its block to the worker on the request it rides, so a sweep of a\nthousand prompts serializes and deserializes the same block a thousand times, and\nonly requests that <em>are</em> nnsight traces are touched at all.</p>\n<p>A registration inverts that. The block goes to the worker once and stays there;\nfrom then on every request the engine runs gets its own copy of it — including\nrequests submitted by something that has never heard of nnsight, an OpenAI-API\nclient on the same server. Each copy keeps its own scope, so what it saves is\nthat request's own, and it comes back on that request's <code>RequestOutput</code> —\n<code>output.saves</code> — by the same collect a traced value uses, then is dropped.</p>"},{"type":"details","summary":"Example","children":[{"type":"html","html":"<blockquote>\n<blockquote>\n<blockquote>\n<p>model = VLLM(\"meta-llama/Llama-3.1-8B\", dispatch=True)</p>\n<p>with model.edit() as (tracer, edit):                    # doctest: +SKIP\n...     hidden = model.model.layers[16].output[0].save()</p>\n<p>outputs = model.vllm_entrypoint.generate(prompts, sampling)  # doctest: +SKIP\noutputs[5].saves[\"hidden\"].shape                        # doctest: +SKIP</p>\n<p>edit.clear()                                            # doctest: +SKIP</p>\n</blockquote>\n</blockquote>\n</blockquote>"}]},{"type":"html","html":"<p>The block is written exactly like a trace body — the same envoy tree, the same\n<code>.save()</code>. What it cannot do is anything that belongs to one particular\nrequest: there is no prompt to invoke, so <code>tracer.invoke(...)</code> has no meaning\nhere, and the block applies to whatever the engine happens to run.</p>\n<p>A prefix-cached token is served without a forward pass, so no hook fires for it\nand the block sees fewer rows than the prompt has, with nothing to say so. A\ntrace asks for its own request to be recomputed; a registration rides requests it\ndid not create and cannot, so nnsight builds its engines with\n<code>enable_prefix_caching=False</code>, and registering against one built with it on\nwarns.</p>"},{"type":"html","html":"<h3 id=\"nnsight.modeling.vllm.registration.Registration\" class=\"doc-heading\">\n<code class=\"doc-symbol doc-symbol-heading doc-symbol-class\"></code>            <span class=\"doc-object-name doc-class-name\">Registration</span>\n\n\n</h3>"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","code":"Registration(model: 'VLLM', id: str, name: str | None = None)"},{"type":"html","html":"<p>A handle on a block the engine is running for every request.</p>\n<p>Returned by <a title=\"            edit\" href=\"/documentation/modeling/vllm/vllm#nnsight.modeling.vllm.vllm.VLLM.edit\"><code>VLLM.edit</code></a> and live\nuntil <code>clear</code>.</p>\n<p>There is nothing to read here. What a registered block saves comes back on\nthe <code>RequestOutput</code> of the request it ran on, as <code>output.saves</code>, by the\nsame collect that carries a traced value — so the values arrive where the\nrequest that produced them already is, and are dropped as they go. Nothing\naccumulates for as long as somebody is reading the outputs, which on the\nsynchronous engine is every request there is.</p>\n<p>A plain <code>with</code> is synchronous-engine only: installing the block is a\n<code>collective_rpc</code>, which on <code>mode=\"async\"</code> is a coroutine there is no safe\nway to finish from a plain statement, so the exit raises there rather than\nsilently not installing it. On an async engine use <code>async with</code> and\n<code>aclear</code>, which can await that trip from inside the loop it is already on.</p>\n\n\n<table>\n      <thead>\n        <tr>\n          <th><span class=\"doc-section-title\">ATTRIBUTE</span></th>\n          <th><span>DESCRIPTION</span></th>\n        </tr>\n      </thead>\n      <tbody>\n          <tr class=\"doc-section-item\">\n            <td><code><a title=\"            model\n\n\n  \n      instance-attribute\n   (nnsight.modeling.vllm.registration.Registration.model)\" href=\"#nnsight.modeling.vllm.registration.Registration.model\">model</a></code></td>\n            <td class=\"doc-attribute-details\">\n              <div class=\"doc-md-description\">\n                <p>The engine this is registered on.</p>\n              </div>\n              <p>\n              </p>\n            </td>\n          </tr>\n          <tr class=\"doc-section-item\">\n            <td><code><a title=\"            id\n\n\n  \n      instance-attribute\n   (nnsight.modeling.vllm.registration.Registration.id)\" href=\"#nnsight.modeling.vllm.registration.Registration.id\">id</a></code></td>\n            <td class=\"doc-attribute-details\">\n              <div class=\"doc-md-description\">\n                <p>The engine-wide id for this registration, used to address it in the\nworker.</p>\n              </div>\n              <p>\n              </p>\n            </td>\n          </tr>\n          <tr class=\"doc-section-item\">\n            <td><code><a title=\"            name\n\n\n  \n      instance-attribute\n   (nnsight.modeling.vllm.registration.Registration.name)\" href=\"#nnsight.modeling.vllm.registration.Registration.name\">name</a></code></td>\n            <td class=\"doc-attribute-details\">\n              <div class=\"doc-md-description\">\n                <p>The name it was installed under, or <code>None</code>. A request that asks\nfor particular edits (<code>edits=[...]</code>) runs the named ones it lists\nand every unnamed one; a request that asks for none runs them all.</p>\n              </div>\n              <p>\n              </p>\n            </td>\n          </tr>\n      </tbody>\n    </table>"},{"type":"html","html":"<h4 id=\"nnsight.modeling.vllm.registration.Registration.model\" class=\"doc-heading\">\n<code class=\"doc-symbol doc-symbol-heading doc-symbol-attribute\"></code>            <span class=\"doc-object-name doc-attribute-name\">model</span>\n\n\n  <span class=\"doc-labels\">\n      <small class=\"doc-label doc-label-instance-attribute\"><code>instance-attribute</code></small>\n  </span>\n\n</h4>"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","code":"model = model"},{"type":"html","html":"<div class=\"doc-contents\">\n\n    </div>"},{"type":"html","html":"<h4 id=\"nnsight.modeling.vllm.registration.Registration.id\" class=\"doc-heading\">\n<code class=\"doc-symbol doc-symbol-heading doc-symbol-attribute\"></code>            <span class=\"doc-object-name doc-attribute-name\">id</span>\n\n\n  <span class=\"doc-labels\">\n      <small class=\"doc-label doc-label-instance-attribute\"><code>instance-attribute</code></small>\n  </span>\n\n</h4>"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","code":"id = id"},{"type":"html","html":"<div class=\"doc-contents\">\n\n    </div>"},{"type":"html","html":"<h4 id=\"nnsight.modeling.vllm.registration.Registration.name\" class=\"doc-heading\">\n<code class=\"doc-symbol doc-symbol-heading doc-symbol-attribute\"></code>            <span class=\"doc-object-name doc-attribute-name\">name</span>\n\n\n  <span class=\"doc-labels\">\n      <small class=\"doc-label doc-label-instance-attribute\"><code>instance-attribute</code></small>\n  </span>\n\n</h4>"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","code":"name = name"},{"type":"html","html":"<div class=\"doc-contents\">\n\n    </div>"},{"type":"html","html":"<h4 id=\"nnsight.modeling.vllm.registration.Registration.cleared\" class=\"doc-heading\">\n<code class=\"doc-symbol doc-symbol-heading doc-symbol-attribute\"></code>            <span class=\"doc-object-name doc-attribute-name\">cleared</span>\n\n\n  <span class=\"doc-labels\">\n      <small class=\"doc-label doc-label-instance-attribute\"><code>instance-attribute</code></small>\n  </span>\n\n</h4>"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","code":"cleared = False"},{"type":"html","html":"<div class=\"doc-contents\">\n\n    </div>"},{"type":"html","html":"<h4 id=\"nnsight.modeling.vllm.registration.Registration.install\" class=\"doc-heading\">\n<code class=\"doc-symbol doc-symbol-heading doc-symbol-method\"></code>            <span class=\"doc-object-name doc-function-name\">install</span>\n\n\n</h4>"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","code":"install(payload: bytes) -> None"},{"type":"html","html":"<div class=\"doc-contents\">\n\n        <p>Put the block on the engine. The seam a serve client replaces.</p>\n\n\n    </div>"},{"type":"html","html":"<h4 id=\"nnsight.modeling.vllm.registration.Registration.ainstall\" class=\"doc-heading\">\n<code class=\"doc-symbol doc-symbol-heading doc-symbol-method\"></code>            <span class=\"doc-object-name doc-function-name\">ainstall</span>\n\n\n  <span class=\"doc-labels\">\n      <small class=\"doc-label doc-label-async\"><code>async</code></small>\n  </span>\n\n</h4>"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","code":"ainstall(payload: bytes) -> None"},{"type":"html","html":"<div class=\"doc-contents\">\n\n        <p><code>install</code>, awaited.</p>\n\n\n    </div>"},{"type":"html","html":"<h4 id=\"nnsight.modeling.vllm.registration.Registration.uninstall\" class=\"doc-heading\">\n<code class=\"doc-symbol doc-symbol-heading doc-symbol-method\"></code>            <span class=\"doc-object-name doc-function-name\">uninstall</span>\n\n\n</h4>"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","code":"uninstall() -> None"},{"type":"html","html":"<div class=\"doc-contents\">\n\n        <p>Take the block off the engine. The other half of the seam.</p>\n\n\n    </div>"},{"type":"html","html":"<h4 id=\"nnsight.modeling.vllm.registration.Registration.auninstall\" class=\"doc-heading\">\n<code class=\"doc-symbol doc-symbol-heading doc-symbol-method\"></code>            <span class=\"doc-object-name doc-function-name\">auninstall</span>\n\n\n  <span class=\"doc-labels\">\n      <small class=\"doc-label doc-label-async\"><code>async</code></small>\n  </span>\n\n</h4>"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","code":"auninstall() -> None"},{"type":"html","html":"<div class=\"doc-contents\">\n\n        <p><code>uninstall</code>, awaited.</p>\n\n\n    </div>"},{"type":"html","html":"<h4 id=\"nnsight.modeling.vllm.registration.Registration.clear\" class=\"doc-heading\">\n<code class=\"doc-symbol doc-symbol-heading doc-symbol-method\"></code>            <span class=\"doc-object-name doc-function-name\">clear</span>\n\n\n</h4>"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","code":"clear() -> None"},{"type":"html","html":"<div class=\"doc-contents\">\n\n        <p>Stop running the block and drop anything it has not handed back.</p>\n<p>Use <code>aclear</code> on an async engine, whose workers can only be reached from\ninside the loop.</p>\n\n\n    </div>"},{"type":"html","html":"<h4 id=\"nnsight.modeling.vllm.registration.Registration.aclear\" class=\"doc-heading\">\n<code class=\"doc-symbol doc-symbol-heading doc-symbol-method\"></code>            <span class=\"doc-object-name doc-function-name\">aclear</span>\n\n\n  <span class=\"doc-labels\">\n      <small class=\"doc-label doc-label-async\"><code>async</code></small>\n  </span>\n\n</h4>"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","code":"aclear() -> None"},{"type":"html","html":"<div class=\"doc-contents\">\n\n        <p><code>clear</code>, awaited — the async engine's form.</p>\n\n\n    </div>"},{"type":"html","html":"<h4 id=\"nnsight.modeling.vllm.registration.Registration.__repr__\" class=\"doc-heading\">\n<code class=\"doc-symbol doc-symbol-heading doc-symbol-method\"></code>            <span class=\"doc-object-name doc-function-name\">__repr__</span>\n\n\n</h4>"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","code":"__repr__() -> str"},{"type":"html","html":"<div class=\"doc-contents\">\n\n\n    </div>"},{"type":"html","html":"<h3 id=\"nnsight.modeling.vllm.registration.ServeRegistration\" class=\"doc-heading\">\n<code class=\"doc-symbol doc-symbol-heading doc-symbol-class\"></code>            <span class=\"doc-object-name doc-class-name\">ServeRegistration</span>\n\n\n</h3>"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","code":"ServeRegistration(model: 'VLLM', id: str, host: str, api_key: str | None = None, name: str | None = None)"},{"type":"html","html":"<p class=\"doc-class-bases\">\n              Bases: <code><a title=\"            Registration (nnsight.modeling.vllm.registration.Registration)\" href=\"#nnsight.modeling.vllm.registration.Registration\">Registration</a></code></p>\n\n\n\n        <p>A block installed on an <a title=\"            server\" href=\"/documentation/modeling/vllm/serve/server#nnsight.modeling.vllm.serve.server\">nnsight-serve</a> engine.</p>\n<p>The same handle, over HTTP: the client has no engine to <code>collective_rpc</code>\ninto — it holds a meta model and no weights — so the block goes to the\nserver, which installs it on the engine it holds. What it saves rides the\nrequest it ran on, which for a serve client means <code>tracer.result.saves</code> of\na trace sent to that same server.</p>"},{"type":"html","html":"<h4 id=\"nnsight.modeling.vllm.registration.ServeRegistration.host\" class=\"doc-heading\">\n<code class=\"doc-symbol doc-symbol-heading doc-symbol-attribute\"></code>            <span class=\"doc-object-name doc-attribute-name\">host</span>\n\n\n  <span class=\"doc-labels\">\n      <small class=\"doc-label doc-label-instance-attribute\"><code>instance-attribute</code></small>\n  </span>\n\n</h4>"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","code":"host = host.rstrip('/')"},{"type":"html","html":"<div class=\"doc-contents\">\n\n    </div>"},{"type":"html","html":"<h4 id=\"nnsight.modeling.vllm.registration.ServeRegistration.api_key\" class=\"doc-heading\">\n<code class=\"doc-symbol doc-symbol-heading doc-symbol-attribute\"></code>            <span class=\"doc-object-name doc-attribute-name\">api_key</span>\n\n\n  <span class=\"doc-labels\">\n      <small class=\"doc-label doc-label-instance-attribute\"><code>instance-attribute</code></small>\n  </span>\n\n</h4>"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","code":"api_key = api_key"},{"type":"html","html":"<div class=\"doc-contents\">\n\n    </div>"},{"type":"html","html":"<h4 id=\"nnsight.modeling.vllm.registration.ServeRegistration.install\" class=\"doc-heading\">\n<code class=\"doc-symbol doc-symbol-heading doc-symbol-method\"></code>            <span class=\"doc-object-name doc-function-name\">install</span>\n\n\n</h4>"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","code":"install(payload: bytes) -> None"},{"type":"html","html":"<div class=\"doc-contents\">\n\n\n    </div>"},{"type":"html","html":"<h4 id=\"nnsight.modeling.vllm.registration.ServeRegistration.ainstall\" class=\"doc-heading\">\n<code class=\"doc-symbol doc-symbol-heading doc-symbol-method\"></code>            <span class=\"doc-object-name doc-function-name\">ainstall</span>\n\n\n  <span class=\"doc-labels\">\n      <small class=\"doc-label doc-label-async\"><code>async</code></small>\n  </span>\n\n</h4>"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","code":"ainstall(payload: bytes) -> None"},{"type":"html","html":"<div class=\"doc-contents\">\n\n\n    </div>"},{"type":"html","html":"<h4 id=\"nnsight.modeling.vllm.registration.ServeRegistration.uninstall\" class=\"doc-heading\">\n<code class=\"doc-symbol doc-symbol-heading doc-symbol-method\"></code>            <span class=\"doc-object-name doc-function-name\">uninstall</span>\n\n\n</h4>"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","code":"uninstall() -> None"},{"type":"html","html":"<div class=\"doc-contents\">\n\n\n    </div>"},{"type":"html","html":"<h4 id=\"nnsight.modeling.vllm.registration.ServeRegistration.auninstall\" class=\"doc-heading\">\n<code class=\"doc-symbol doc-symbol-heading doc-symbol-method\"></code>            <span class=\"doc-object-name doc-function-name\">auninstall</span>\n\n\n  <span class=\"doc-labels\">\n      <small class=\"doc-label doc-label-async\"><code>async</code></small>\n  </span>\n\n</h4>"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","code":"auninstall() -> None"},{"type":"html","html":"<div class=\"doc-contents\">\n\n\n    </div>"},{"type":"html","html":"<h4 id=\"nnsight.modeling.vllm.registration.ServeRegistration.__repr__\" class=\"doc-heading\">\n<code class=\"doc-symbol doc-symbol-heading doc-symbol-method\"></code>            <span class=\"doc-object-name doc-function-name\">__repr__</span>\n\n\n</h4>"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","code":"__repr__() -> str"},{"type":"html","html":"<div class=\"doc-contents\">\n\n\n    </div>"},{"type":"html","html":"<h3 id=\"nnsight.modeling.vllm.registration.RegisteringTracer\" class=\"doc-heading\">\n<code class=\"doc-symbol doc-symbol-heading doc-symbol-class\"></code>            <span class=\"doc-object-name doc-class-name\">RegisteringTracer</span>\n\n\n</h3>"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","code":"RegisteringTracer(model: 'VLLM', *, backend: Backend | None = None, serve: str | None = None, api_key: str | None = None, name: str | None = None)"},{"type":"html","html":"<p class=\"doc-class-bases\">\n              Bases: <code><a title=\"            VLLMTracer (nnsight.modeling.vllm.tracer.VLLMTracer)\" href=\"/documentation/modeling/vllm/tracer#nnsight.modeling.vllm.tracer.VLLMTracer\">VLLMTracer</a></code></p>\n\n\n\n        <p>Capture a block and leave it on the engine instead of running it once.</p>\n<p>The counterpart of <a title=\"            EditingTracer\" href=\"/documentation/intervention/editing#nnsight.intervention.editing.EditingTracer\"><code>EditingTracer</code></a>\nfor a runtime whose model lives in another process: an edit is replayed by\nthe envoy that stores it, which on vLLM would leave it in the client, where\nthere are no weights. This sends the block across instead, and hands back a\n<a title=\"            Registration\" href=\"#nnsight.modeling.vllm.registration.Registration\"><code>Registration</code></a> to switch it\noff again with.</p>"},{"type":"html","html":"<h4 id=\"nnsight.modeling.vllm.registration.RegisteringTracer.registration\" class=\"doc-heading\">\n<code class=\"doc-symbol doc-symbol-heading doc-symbol-attribute\"></code>            <span class=\"doc-object-name doc-attribute-name\">registration</span>\n\n\n  <span class=\"doc-labels\">\n      <small class=\"doc-label doc-label-instance-attribute\"><code>instance-attribute</code></small>\n  </span>\n\n</h4>"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","code":"registration: Registration | None = None"},{"type":"html","html":"<div class=\"doc-contents\">\n\n    </div>"},{"type":"html","html":"<h4 id=\"nnsight.modeling.vllm.registration.RegisteringTracer.__enter__\" class=\"doc-heading\">\n<code class=\"doc-symbol doc-symbol-heading doc-symbol-method\"></code>            <span class=\"doc-object-name doc-function-name\">__enter__</span>\n\n\n</h4>"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","code":"__enter__() -> tuple['RegisteringTracer', Registration]"},{"type":"html","html":"<p>Enter the block, binding the tracer and the handle that ends it.</p>\n<p>Both, the way <a title=\"            edit\" href=\"/documentation/intervention/envoy#nnsight.intervention.envoy.Envoy.edit\"><code>Envoy.edit</code></a> binds\n<code>(tracer, edited)</code>: a registered block is still a trace body, and the\ntracer is what carries <code>iter</code>/<code>all</code>, without which the block could\nonly ever see a request's first forward — its prefill — and never the\nsteps it generates::</p>"},{"type":"code","lang":"text","code":"with model.edit() as (tracer, edit):\n    readouts = nnsight.save([])\n    for step in tracer.all():\n        readouts.append(model.model.layers[16].output[0][-1])"},{"type":"html","html":"<h4 id=\"nnsight.modeling.vllm.registration.RegisteringTracer.__aenter__\" class=\"doc-heading\">\n<code class=\"doc-symbol doc-symbol-heading doc-symbol-method\"></code>            <span class=\"doc-object-name doc-function-name\">__aenter__</span>\n\n\n  <span class=\"doc-labels\">\n      <small class=\"doc-label doc-label-async\"><code>async</code></small>\n  </span>\n\n</h4>"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","code":"__aenter__() -> tuple['RegisteringTracer', Registration]"},{"type":"html","html":"<div class=\"doc-contents\">\n\n        <p><code>__enter__</code>, for <code>async with</code> — the form an async engine needs.</p>\n<p>Spelled out rather than delegating to <code>__enter__</code>: both <code>capture</code> and the\nskip guard read the caller's frame at a fixed depth, so going through\nanother call would hand them this method's frame — <code>capture</code> would find no\n<code>with</code> block at all, and <code>skip_context</code> would arm the wrong frame and\nlet the body run here as well as on the workers.</p>\n\n\n    </div>"},{"type":"html","html":"<h4 id=\"nnsight.modeling.vllm.registration.RegisteringTracer.__exit__\" class=\"doc-heading\">\n<code class=\"doc-symbol doc-symbol-heading doc-symbol-method\"></code>            <span class=\"doc-object-name doc-function-name\">__exit__</span>\n\n\n</h4>"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","code":"__exit__(*exception: Any) -> bool"},{"type":"html","html":"<div class=\"doc-contents\">\n\n\n    </div>"},{"type":"html","html":"<h4 id=\"nnsight.modeling.vllm.registration.RegisteringTracer.__aexit__\" class=\"doc-heading\">\n<code class=\"doc-symbol doc-symbol-heading doc-symbol-method\"></code>            <span class=\"doc-object-name doc-function-name\">__aexit__</span>\n\n\n  <span class=\"doc-labels\">\n      <small class=\"doc-label doc-label-async\"><code>async</code></small>\n  </span>\n\n</h4>"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","code":"__aexit__(*exception: Any) -> bool"},{"type":"html","html":"<div class=\"doc-contents\">\n\n        <p>Capture as usual, then await the send.</p>\n<p>The block is prepared by <code>execute</code> either way; only the trip to the\nworkers differs, and on an async engine that trip has to be awaited from\ninside the loop.</p>\n\n\n    </div>"},{"type":"html","html":"<h4 id=\"nnsight.modeling.vllm.registration.RegisteringTracer.execute\" class=\"doc-heading\">\n<code class=\"doc-symbol doc-symbol-heading doc-symbol-method\"></code>            <span class=\"doc-object-name doc-function-name\">execute</span>\n\n\n</h4>"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","code":"execute(code: CodeType) -> None"},{"type":"html","html":"<div class=\"doc-contents\">\n\n        <p>Prepare the block for the workers rather than running it here.</p>\n<p>Only prepared: the send happens in <code>__exit__</code>/<code>__aexit__</code>, because\nwhether it can be awaited depends on which of the two ran.</p>\n<p>It goes to every rank, so each builds the same per-request copies and\ntheir reads stay in step — which is what a sharded model's gathers need.</p>\n<p><code>copy</code> is left off: the worker builds a fresh mediator per request from\nthis template, so each request already has a scope of its own, and the\nblock's saves have to land in it for the collect to find them.</p>\n\n\n    </div>"}]}